+# replay-orders
+
+A small orders service. It lists and reads orders over HTTP, keeps them in an in-memory SQLite
+database, and writes an audit line for every order event it publishes.
+
+- The HTTP contract is [docs/api.md](docs/api.md); change it in the same change as the code.
+- Configuration lives in `config/service.json` and is validated by `src/config/load.ts`.
+- There are no runtime dependencies: `node:http` serves, `node:sqlite` stores.
+
+## Develop
+
+Node 22.13 or later (`node:sqlite` without a flag).
+
+```sh
+npm install
+npm run lint
+npm run typecheck
+npm test
+```
+
+## Run
+
+`node src/server.ts` on Node 22.18 or later, which runs TypeScript directly. It listens on
+`PORT` (default 8080), accepts the comma-separated bearer tokens in `ORDERS_TOKENS`, and serves
+invoices from `ORDERS_INVOICE_DIR` (default `invoices`).
+
+## Layout
+
+| Path | What it holds |
+|---|---|
+| `src/http/` | the router, the request pipeline and the route table |
+| `src/auth/` | the bearer-token guard |
+| `src/orders/` | the order handlers, the wire shape and the text formatting |
+| `src/store/` | the database and its queries |
+| `src/reports/` | reporting helpers such as time windows |
+| `src/events/` | order events and the audit trail that consumes them |
+| `src/config/` | configuration defaults and validation |
+| `test/` | vitest suites; `test/helpers.ts` starts the app on a free port |
