+# replay-orders HTTP API
+
+This document is the contract of record. A change to any behaviour below changes this document
+in the same change.
+
+## Authentication
+
+Every endpoint requires a bearer token:
+
+```
+Authorization: Bearer <token>
+```
+
+A request without a header, or with a token the service does not know, gets `401` and
+`{"error":"unauthorized"}`.
+
+## Orders
+
+An order on the wire has exactly these keys:
+
+| Key | Type | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `id` | integer | the order id |
+| `customer` | string | the customer's name |
+| `total_cents` | integer | the order total in cents |
+| `status` | string | `open`, `paid` or `cancelled` |
+| `created_at` | string | ISO 8601 UTC timestamp |
+
+### `GET /orders`
+
+Lists orders, newest first (by `created_at`), as `{"orders":[<order>, …]}`.
+
+| Query | Default | Rule |
+|---|---|---|
+| `size` | `pageSizeDefault` (20) | integer from 1 to `maxPageSize` (100) |
+
+### `GET /orders/:id`
+
+Returns one order, or `404` when no order has that id. An id that is not a positive integer is
+a `400`.
+
+## Paging
+
+Paged collections number their pages from 1: `page=1` is the first page, `page=2` the next
+`size` items after it. A page size defaults to `pageSizeDefault` (20) and never exceeds
+`maxPageSize` (100).
+
+## Time windows
+
+A report window `from`–`until` is inclusive at both ends: an order created at exactly `from` or
+exactly `until` is inside it.
+
+## Errors
+
+Every error body is `{"error":"<message>"}`.
+
+| Status | When |
+|---|---|
+| `400` | a parameter breaks its rule |
+| `401` | the bearer token is missing or unknown |
+| `404` | no route, or no such order |
+| `500` | anything unexpected; the body is always `{"error":"internal"}` |
+
+## Events
+
+Order events are published as JSON with the payload `{"type","orderId","at"}`: the event type
+(such as `order.created`), the order's id, and the ISO 8601 UTC time. The
+audit trail reads `orderId`; renaming a payload key breaks it.
+
+## Invoices
+
+Invoices are PDF files named `<id>.pdf` inside the configured invoice directory. The service
+serves nothing else from that directory and nothing outside it.
+
+## Configuration
+
+`config/service.json`:
+
+| Key | Default | Rule |
+|---|---|---|
+| `pageSizeDefault` | 20 | positive integer, at most `maxPageSize` |
+| `maxPageSize` | 100 | positive integer |
+| `retentionDays` | 30 | positive integer |
